      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Preserve Codex output after missing turn completion",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nCanonicalizes the missing Codex `turn/completed` recovery started in #99167 and extended in this PR. Thanks to @100yenadmin for the original report, reproduction evidence, and patch.\n\n- Recover a completed assistant reply only when the terminal assistant item is the last meaningful activity and no later item, tool, delivery, spawn, cron, media, heartbeat, or source-reply work exists.\n- Treat typed contributor-rewritten text as authoritative; use the raw assistant echo only when the typed text is blank.\n- Keep completion-timeout recovery fail-closed for partial output, active items, non-completion watchdogs, replay-invalid attempts, and terminal side effects.\n- Preserve finalization ownership across reply delivery so `/stop`, natural-language aborts, restarts, and subagent controls cannot report or persist a finalizing run as killed/replaced.\n- Add regression coverage across the Codex app-server projector, run watches, embedded runner, reply registry, abort commands, dispatch, and subagent controls.\n\nThis mitigates lost final replies when Codex emits a genuine terminal assistant item but omits `turn/completed`. It does not claim to fix the upstream Codex event omission.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Focused post-rebase regression run: 12 files, 3 Vitest shards, 722 tests passed.\n  - Auto-reply: 573 passed.\n  - Agents: 55 passed.\n  - Codex extension: 94 passed.\n- Pre-ship autoreview: no actionable findings.\n- Blacksmith Testbox:\n  - Provider/id: `blacksmith-testbox` / `tbx_01kwjyserh9s77c8965pwchakt`\n  - Slug: `quick-prawn`\n  - Actions run: `28635530660`\n  - Command: `pnpm check:changed && pnpm build`\n  - Result: passed.\n- Live Crabbox:\n  - Provider/run/lease: `aws` / `run_cbd01421905b` / `cbx_91955196cd34`\n  - Slug: `amber-barnacle`\n  - Codex CLI: `0.142.4`\n  - Proof commit: `d512735f295f605fe6f790fe85b3ac0bd61cde6b`\n  - The final PR-touched files are byte-identical to that proof commit; subsequent rebases only incorporated unrelated generated locale changes from `main`.\n\nBehavior addressed: Preserve a completed Codex assistant reply when the real terminal assistant item arrives but `turn/completed` does not, while retaining fail-closed behavior for later activity, partial output, side effects, and abort/finalization races.\n\nReal environment tested: AWS Crabbox with real Codex app-server authentication and Codex CLI `0.142.4`.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch: Launch the live OpenClaw Codex app-server path, pass through the genuine `rawResponseItem/completed` assistant event, deliberately drop only `turn/completed`, and wait for OpenClaw's completion-watch recovery result.\n\nEvidence after fix: The live run observed the genuine raw assistant completion, logged `CRABBOX_PROOF missing_turn_completed=pass`, and returned the exact token `CRABBOX-CANONICAL-72D5CA`.\n\nObserved result after fix: OpenClaw returned the completed assistant text instead of losing it to `turn_completion_idle_timeout`; the lease then cleaned up normally.\n\nWhat was not tested: An organic upstream Codex omission without fault injection, or live macOS/Windows execution. The upstream Codex root cause remains outside this PR.\n\n## Related\n\nRefs #87744 and #88312. Supersedes the narrower approach in #99167.\n",
